From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: tegra: handle unconfigured optional GMSL inputs

The modular EDGEDES transport overlay describes four possible GMSL inputs.
A camera leaf overlay supplies the remote endpoint only for its selected
port. Inputs without a leaf intentionally have no remote-endpoint property.
The VI graph parser resolves every remote before filtering Maxim output
pads and unrelated optional inputs, so one unconfigured input aborts graph
parsing for every VI channel, including channels with a connected camera.

Classify Maxim endpoints and select the channel's physical input before
resolving its remote parent. Skip a missing remote-endpoint property only
on an input of a bridge that opts into compulab,allow-missing-links. Keep
remote resolution mandatory for configured inputs: a present but invalid
remote-endpoint property still reports an error. Ordinary sensor graphs
retain their strict remote requirement, and Maxim CSI output endpoints
remain excluded from upstream traversal.

No remote node reference is acquired for an endpoint filtered before
resolution, so remove the corresponding of_node_put calls. References for
traversed upstream entities continue to follow the existing ownership.
Do not change sensor modes, device-tree composition or Argus/NITO policy.

Prepared against NVIDIA Jetson Linux 39.2.1 after the ADI patches
0100 through 0103.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab Tegra optional camera discovery]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
---
 drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c | 32 +++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
@@ -678,15 +678,11 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_parse_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 
 		dev_dbg(chan->vi->dev, "handling endpoint %s\n", ep->full_name);
 
-		remote = of_graph_get_remote_port_parent(ep);
-		if (!remote) {
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			break;
-		}
-
 		/* Only walk upstream of a Maxim bridge, not another CSI channel. */
 		if (tegra_vi_graph_is_maxim_deserializer(node)) {
 			struct of_endpoint endpoint;
+			bool optional = of_property_read_bool(node,
+						"compulab,allow-missing-links");
 			u32 num_links = 4;
 
 			if (of_device_is_compatible(node, "maxim,max9296a"))
@@ -696,21 +692,23 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_parse_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 				num_links = 1;
 
 			ret = of_graph_parse_endpoint(ep, &endpoint);
-			if (ret) {
-				of_node_put(remote);
+			if (ret)
 				break;
-			}
-			if (endpoint.port >= num_links) {
-				of_node_put(remote);
+			if (endpoint.port >= num_links)
 				continue;
-			}
 			/* Each optional capture channel owns only its input graph. */
-			if (of_property_read_bool(node,
-						  "compulab,allow-missing-links") &&
-			    endpoint.port != chan->virtual_channel) {
-				of_node_put(remote);
+			if (optional && endpoint.port != chan->virtual_channel)
+				continue;
+			/* No leaf overlay configured this optional input. */
+			if (optional &&
+			    !of_find_property(ep, "remote-endpoint", NULL))
 				continue;
-			}
+		}
+
+		remote = of_graph_get_remote_port_parent(ep);
+		if (!remote) {
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			break;
 		}
 
 		/* skip the vi of_node and duplicated entities */
-- 
